### How often does it reproduce? Is there a required condition?

Reproduces 100% of the time in Node v24.11.1 when logging ZodError objects from the zod library (v3.23.8).
Required conditions:

- Node.js version must be 24.11.1 (does NOT reproduce in 24.11.0)
- Error object must be a ZodError from the zod library

This appears to be a regression introduced in Node 24.11.1.

### What is the expected behavior? Why is that the expected behavior?

console.error() should successfully format and log the error object without crashing, just as it does in Node 24.11.0 and earlier versions.

