remove file 1
```

### What alternatives have you considered?

### Prior Art

### C

https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/program/atexit

```c
int atexit( void (*func)(void) );
```

> The functions will be called in reverse order they were registered, i.e. the function registered last will be executed first.

### Python

https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/atexit.html#module-atexit

```python
atexit.register(func, *args, **kwargs)
atexit.unregister(func)
```

> atexit runs these functions in the reverse order in which they were registered; if you register A, B, and C, at interpreter termination time they will be run in the order C, B, A.

